# Act 2, chapter 6 "Taken": the walk home at night (areas from log4/gen_ch6.py, world 16). Gero's machines are
# sweeping the city; the twins head for the warehouse at the docks, where the Collector is waiting, then the drones.
# Flags: 333 home intro, 334 Collector destroyed (its death script), 335 / 336 caches, 337 crossroads; 305 ambush.
list night_crossroads
set_flag 337
do begin_moves; move drone_night_a 424 300; wait_moves
narrate A drone drifts low over the crossroads. A red beam sweeps the street, slow and careful.
say lazuli.0 Don't move.
narrate The beam slides across the twins' shoes... and moves on.
say lapis.1 That thing's looking for someone.
say lazuli.0 For two someones. Down the south road. Now.
do begin_moves; move drone_night_a 424 150; wait_moves
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch6_home
set_flag 333
narrate The old warehouse. The Red Fangs are long gone. The door hangs open.
say lapis.2 Home sweet home.
say lazuli.0 Lapis... we closed that door this afternoon.
narrate Something heavy shifts in the dark between the crates. Metal grinds on concrete.
say lapis.1 The man in the coat sent a bigger dog.
journal Destroy the {c07}machine{c02} in the warehouse
do call 47; call 51 0
list night_cache_river
if_flag 335 nriver_empty
set_flag 335
narrate The rowboat again. Someone stashed a bottle of root beer under the seat since this afternoon.
do call 129 5 1
stop
label nriver_empty
narrate Just the rowboat.
list night_cache_docks
if_flag 336 ndocks_empty
set_flag 336
narrate The dome house. Whoever lived here left in a hurry: a half-eaten meal and a Senzu Bean on the table.
do call 129 11 1
stop
label ndocks_empty
narrate The dome house is dark and empty.
# ---------- the searchlights and the old house (log4/gen_more.py; flags 470 south road seen, 471 the memory,
# 472 rooftop chase, 473 rooftop hunter destroyed (its death script reloads the roof), 474 house cache)
list night_spotted
narrate A red beam snaps onto Lazuli's face.
narrate Drone (flat voice): Subject sighted. Subject sighted.
say lapis.1 Back! Into the park, now!
narrate They don't stop running until they're under the trees. The beams go back to sweeping the road.
say lazuli.0 There's a gap where the beams don't meet. South of the crossroads. We go through there, together.
do call 120 20; call 119 16 1 1 112 480; call 121 20
do call 47; call 51 0
list night_south
set_flag 470
narrate Two drones hang over the south bridge, their beams crossing on the road. Nobody is getting past them.
say lapis.1 Not that way. The houses. Over the roofs.
do call 120 20; call 119 16 1 1 420 600; call 121 20
do call 47; call 51 0
list ch6_oldhouse
set_flag 471
narrate Their old house. The door was never locked. There was never anything worth taking.
narrate Dust on everything. Mom's chair by the window. A television that stopped working before they left.
say lazuli.0 Lapis, look. The doorframe.
narrate Pencil marks, climbing the wood. L and L, age six. Age seven. Age eight. Then nothing.
say lapis.2 You always stood on your toes.
say lazuli.3 I did not. ...Once. Maybe twice.
say lapis.1 After Mom, they wanted to split us up. Two families. Two different cities.
say lazuli.0 We left the same night. You carried the bag. I carried you for the second half.
say lapis.2 I was tired. I was eight.
narrate A red light slides across the window. Then another. Then the glass blows inward.
narrate Drone: Subjects located. Begin retrieval.
say lazuli.0 The roof! The ladder, the hatch!
do call 120 20; call 119 16 47 1 56 124; call 121 20
journal Run for the {c07}fire stairs{c02} across the rooftops
do call 47; call 51 0
list house_ladder
unless_flag 471 ladder_early
narrate The hatch to the roof. They used to sit up there on summer nights and count the airships.
do call 120 20; call 119 16 47 1 56 124; call 121 20
do call 47; call 51 0
stop
label ladder_early
narrate A ladder in the corner, up to a hatch in the ceiling. It leads to the roof.
list cache_house
if_flag 474 chouse_empty
set_flag 474
narrate Lapis's old shoebox, still under the bed. A slingshot. A comic with no cover. A can of cherry soda he was saving for a special day.
say lapis.2 I guess this is the special day.
do call 129 4 1
stop
label chouse_empty
narrate The empty shoebox. Lapis kept the slingshot.
list roof_chase_1
set_flag 472
narrate Behind them, a drone rises over the edge of the roof. Its beam lights up the whole ledge.
say lazuli.0 It's right behind us. The fire stairs, at the far end. Go!
narrate Another one drops out of the sky ahead of them, onto the fire stairs, with a heavy clang. Its guns are already out.
say lapis.1 That one's not here to take us home.
journal Get past the {c07}hunter{c02} on the fire stairs
do call 47; call 51 0
list roof_stairs_blocked
narrate The hunter drone is planted on the fire stairs. There's no way down while it's there.
# ---------- Gero's note 3 (flag 522)
list note_house
if_flag 522 nhouse_read
set_flag 522
narrate On top of the broken television: a notebook page, placed there neatly. The dust around it is fresh.
narrate "Subjects' former residence. Mother deceased. Father unknown. The twins ran from the children's home rather than be separated."
narrate "Their loyalty to each other is excessive. Correctable."
say lazuli.0 He's been in our house, Lapis. He stood right here.
say lapis.1 Then he can come back and say it to my face.
do call 129 31 1
run notes_check
stop
label nhouse_read
narrate The dead television. Lazuli doesn't look at it.
# ---------- Mrs. Oda (second length pass, log4/gen_more.py ch6_jobs; 531 met, 532 bag found, 533 returned)
list mrs_oda
if_flag 533 oda_after
if_flag 531 oda_waiting
set_flag 531
narrate An old woman sits under the bridge on a flattened box, a blanket round her shoulders.
narrate Old woman: Who's there? ...No. No, it can't be. Lapis? Little Lazuli?
say lazuli.0 Mrs. Oda? From downstairs?
narrate Mrs. Oda: The very same. The Red Fangs took the building after you two ran off. Took everyone's rooms, one by one.
say lapis.1 You're sleeping out here? In this?
narrate Mrs. Oda: Those flying machines came through tonight. I ran, and I dropped my bag by the docks. Everything I have left is in it.
if_flag 532 oda_waiting
narrate Mrs. Oda: The fence by the dome house, I think. I didn't dare go back.
say lazuli.3 We'll get it. Stay here.
stop
label oda_waiting
unless_flag 532 oda_wait
set_flag 533
narrate Mrs. Oda: My bag! Oh, you good children. You always were, whatever the building said.
narrate She takes out a photograph, bent at the corners, and holds it out to Lazuli.
narrate Mrs. Oda: Your mother gave me this to keep, the winter she got sick. She said, "If they ever come back, give it to them." So. You came back.
say lazuli.0 That's us. And her. I'd forgotten her hair was like that.
say lapis.2 You hadn't. You just stopped saying it.
narrate Mrs. Oda: Go on, now. Whatever's chasing you, don't let it catch you standing still.
do call 129 0 2; call 129 11 1
narrate Got 2 Milks and a Senzu Bean.
stop
label oda_wait
narrate Mrs. Oda: The fence by the dome house at the docks. A grey cloth bag. Be careful of those machines.
stop
label oda_after
narrate Mrs. Oda: (holding her bag close) Go on, both of you. Stay together.
list oda_bag
if_flag 532 oda_bag_taken
set_flag 532
narrate A grey cloth bag hangs off the fence, torn on one corner. A tin cup, a blanket, a bundle of letters.
unless_flag 531 oda_bag_stranger
say lazuli.0 Mrs. Oda's. Let's get it back to her.
stop
label oda_bag_stranger
say lapis.1 Someone dropped everything they own. Hang on to it, maybe they're nearby.
stop
label oda_bag_taken
narrate A white fence. Nothing hanging off it now.
